{"id": "msg_1664", "user_name": "meme-benchmark", "session_id": "27c744c6-eea0-4f7e-a3f4-5fa49e27d0e9", "role": "user", "message": "How can non-accredited investors invest in Open AI?Currently, non-accredited investors are not able to directly invest in OpenAI. The company is privately held and its shares are not publicly traded. The investment opportunities are mostly restricted to accredited investors, venture capital firms, and strategic partners.Accredited investors are individuals or entities that meet certain criteria set forth by the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) in the United States. Generally, this includes having a net worth of over $1 million or having income over $200,000 per year for the past two years.There are few options for the general public to invest in companies like OpenAI and similar, one of which would be investing in companies like NVIDIA and AMD which have many collaborations and partnership with AI startups and companies and are listed in stock market.You may want to consult with a financial advisor to explore other investment options that align with your goals and risk tolerance.1. Would it be possible to start a venture capital company registered outside the US, to source function for Open AI from accredited investors?

